  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB, while it has more than one element, you can apply an operation on it - you choose any two elements x,yx,yx,y  (they may be the same value, but they should have different indices), delete them, and add an element g(x,y)g(x, y)g(x,y) instead.\n\nHere g(x,y)g(x, y)g(x,y) denotes the highest set bit in x⊕yx \\oplus yx⊕y, or 000 if they are equal. In other words, g(x,y)=max⁡2kg(x, y) = \\max 2^kg(x,y)=max2k, such that 2k≤(x⊕y)2^k \\leq (x \\oplus y)2k≤(x⊕y) for x≠yx \\neq yx=y, and g(x,y)=0g(x,y)=0g(x,y)=0 if x=yx = yx=y. For example, g(1,1)=0,g(1,2)=2,g(2,4)=4,g(13,17)=16g(1,1) = 0, g(1,2) = 2, g(2,4)=4, g(13,17)=16g(1,1)=0,g(1,2)=2,g(2,4)=4,g(13,17)=16.\n\nGiven an array BBB, we try to apply the operations repeatedly in such a way that when we are left with only one element at the end, that element is as small as possible. Let's denote this smallest possible value of the element at the end as f(B)f(B)f(B).\n\nYou are given an array AAA with NNN elements, you need to find the sum of f(Al…r)f(A_{l \\ldots r})f(Al…r​) among all subsegments 1≤l≤r≤N1 \\leq l \\leq r \\leq N1≤l≤r≤N.\n\nThe answer may be large, so you need to find it modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line contains one integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n###Output:\r\nIn a single line, print the sum, modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤N≤300 0001 \\leq N \\leq 300\\,0001≤N≤300000\n0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\leq A_i &lt; 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230\n###Subtasks\n\n\n10 points : 1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10\n10 points : 1≤N≤5001 \\leq N \\leq 5001≤N≤500\n10 points : 1≤N≤50001 \\leq N \\leq 50001≤N≤5000\n70 points : 1≤N≤300 0001 \\leq N \\leq 300\\,0001≤N≤300000",
